Secure SDLC and DevSecOps Integration on AWS
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

• Understand the fundamentals of DevSecOps and its integration with AWS security services • Set up a complete DevSecOps pipeline using AWS native tools • Configure AWS Security Hub for centralized security findings management • Implement AWS CodeGuru Reviewer for automated code security analysis • Deploy Amazon GuardDuty for threat detection and monitoring • Utilize AWS Config for compliance monitoring and configuration management • Create Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates using Terraform • Validate Terraform configurations using security scanning tools • Integrate Checkov for policy-as-code security scanning • Implement automated security testing throughout the software development lifecycle

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

• Basic understanding of cloud computing concepts • Familiarity with AWS services and console navigation • Basic knowledge of Git version control • Understanding of CI/CD pipeline concepts • Basic command-line interface experience • Fundamental knowledge of JSON and YAML formats

